<article class="env-definition" id="02AD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02AD">Definition <span data-tag="02AD">111.40.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally ringed space. An <em>invertible ${\mathcal O}_ X$-module</em> on $X$ is a sheaf of ${\mathcal O}_ X$-modules ${\mathcal L}$ such that every point has an open neighbourhood $U \subset X$ such that ${\mathcal L}|_ U$ is isomorphic to ${\mathcal O}_ U$ as ${\mathcal O}_ U$-module. We say that ${\mathcal L}$ is trivial if it is isomorphic to ${\mathcal O}_ X$ as a ${\mathcal O}_ X$-module. </p>
</article>